# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::FevdOptions`

Options of `VarFit::fevd`.

`FevdOptions` selects the horizon and the shock identification of the variance decomposition.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `horizon` | `std::int64_t` | 20 | Number of steps; it must be greater than 0. |
| `method` | `ts::IrfMethod` | `Orthogonalized` | As in `IrfOptions`. For `Generalized` the shares are normalised so each series' shares add up to one. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

